2
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:08,407
The Greatest of Elven-smiths
is consumed by his work.

3
00:00:08,408 --> 00:00:12,199
He asks that I handle all matters
of administration in his stead.

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,907
I'm just fatigued.

5
00:00:13,908 --> 00:00:16,449
You are the Lord of Eregion.
You have responsibilities.

6
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:18,950
Until the Nine are complete,
nothing else matters.

7
00:00:19,075 --> 00:00:20,922
Without mithril, the
remaining Rings of Power

8
00:00:20,923 --> 00:00:21,949
may never be complete.

9
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:23,407
We need more.

10
00:00:23,408 --> 00:00:24,658
The answer is no.

11
00:00:25,283 --> 00:00:27,199
Tell Narvi we're expanding the dig.

12
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,324
Have you gone mad?

13
00:00:28,325 --> 00:00:29,615
Take off the Ring.

14
00:00:29,616 --> 00:00:32,866
I have nothing to prove to you, boy.

15
00:00:35,741 --> 00:00:39,074
We'll lay our bodies in front of
that mine ourselves if we have to.

16
00:00:39,075 --> 00:00:40,075
Disa?

17
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:43,157
The Orcs are not in Mordor.

18
00:00:43,158 --> 00:00:45,533
A legion of them are headed for Eregion.

19
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,282
Galadriel was right.

20
00:00:48,283 --> 00:00:49,699
You must send aid!

21
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:54,741
Our armies cannot defeat both
Adar and Sauron. Not alone.

22
00:00:56,825 --> 00:00:58,324
I brought you here.

23
00:00:58,325 --> 00:01:00,241
For we share a common enemy.

24
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:02,657
Elrond hastens from Lindon

25
00:01:02,658 --> 00:01:04,657
with an army of Elves.

26
00:01:04,658 --> 00:01:07,282
And Nenya, my Ring.

27
00:01:07,283 --> 00:01:10,032
Sauron believes he is
still beyond my grasp.

28
00:01:10,033 --> 00:01:12,408
But I know he hides in Eregion.

29
00:01:14,450 --> 00:01:15,699
How fares your progress?

30
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,282
I cannot forge more
Rings without mithril.

31
00:01:19,283 --> 00:01:20,699
I have been to Khazad-dûm.

32
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:22,324
One-ninth portion.

33
00:01:22,325 --> 00:01:23,783
It should be enough.

34
00:01:25,533 --> 00:01:27,990
Sauron has no army of his own,

35
00:01:27,991 --> 00:01:30,657
so he's lured yours here instead.

36
00:01:30,658 --> 00:01:32,699
He wants you to attack Eregion.

37
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:34,282
Eregion will fall.

38
00:01:34,283 --> 00:01:35,490
And Sauron with it.

39
00:01:35,491 --> 00:01:36,491
Bind her.

40
00:01:36,492 --> 00:01:37,824
No!

41
00:01:37,825 --> 00:01:39,533
This is what Sauron wants!

42
00:02:56,241 --> 00:02:57,533
Nine...

43
00:03:00,158 --> 00:03:01,658
... for mortal Men.

44
00:03:36,241 --> 00:03:37,783
Hello, Mr. Mouse.

45
00:03:50,658 --> 00:03:51,908
Have you fallen?

46
00:03:55,283 --> 00:03:59,074
Come. The floor is hardly the place
for the Greatest of Elven-smiths.

47
00:03:59,075 --> 00:04:00,366
No, I... I, uh...

48
00:04:03,325 --> 00:04:07,658
Fëanor's hammer is, is missing a...

49
00:04:09,991 --> 00:04:11,366
Missing a, a...

50
00:04:12,283 --> 00:04:14,325
You know how forgetful you can be.

51
00:04:16,533 --> 00:04:17,533
No, no.

52
00:04:20,158 --> 00:04:21,575
No, this was different.

53
00:04:23,408 --> 00:04:26,158
I trust you are not
feeling overwhelmed again?

54
00:04:27,491 --> 00:04:28,491
No.

55
00:04:30,241 --> 00:04:32,533
Quite the opposite, in fact.

56
00:04:34,450 --> 00:04:37,365
These past weeks, I
have felt such clarity,

57
00:04:37,366 --> 00:04:40,741
a focus that I have not known in years.

58
00:04:41,658 --> 00:04:43,408
And I have you to thank for that.

59
00:04:44,158 --> 00:04:45,158
Please.

60
00:04:45,741 --> 00:04:47,408
When the world is still,

61
00:04:49,658 --> 00:04:53,991
then the ideas can flow freely.

62
00:04:55,991 --> 00:05:01,616
My work is but to let them
share the secrets of their song.

63
00:05:06,616 --> 00:05:08,325
How fares your progress?

64
00:05:13,241 --> 00:05:15,491
The Rings of Power are nearly complete.

65
00:05:18,783 --> 00:05:19,783
How long?

66
00:05:21,866 --> 00:05:23,490
What is another few days

67
00:05:23,491 --> 00:05:29,116
to perfect something
that shall last forever?

68
00:05:33,033 --> 00:05:35,200
It will be a sad occasion.

69
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:38,991
I have so enjoyed our time together.

70
00:05:40,991 --> 00:05:42,741
Well, all things must end.

71
00:05:46,908 --> 00:05:50,741
A pity. Is it not?

72
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:43,575
It is time.

73
00:06:52,325 --> 00:06:53,325
My lord.

74
00:06:53,326 --> 00:06:55,157
What orders from Lord Celebrimbor?

75
00:06:55,158 --> 00:06:57,575
Lord Celebrimbor refuses
to permit a counter-attack.

76
00:06:58,366 --> 00:07:00,407
He says the river will protect us.

77
00:07:00,408 --> 00:07:02,657
Every moment we remain
idle, more Elves die.

78
00:07:02,658 --> 00:07:03,949
We must do something.

79
00:07:03,950 --> 00:07:05,741
And that is why we're
not going to obey him.

80
00:07:06,991 --> 00:07:08,408
Gather your finest troops.

81
00:07:09,741 --> 00:07:11,575
I am taking command of our defenses.

82
00:07:12,158 --> 00:07:14,282
- Valar bless you, my lord.
- This way. Go!

83
00:07:14,283 --> 00:07:17,408
What is it? What are
you not telling them?

84
00:07:19,783 --> 00:07:21,658
Celebrimbor's mind is gone.

85
00:07:24,950 --> 00:07:26,075
We are alone.

86
00:07:28,908 --> 00:07:29,908
Quickly.

87
00:07:30,533 --> 00:07:31,950
Not alone.

88
00:07:38,325 --> 00:07:41,283
You have proven your quality, Mirdania.

89
00:07:43,033 --> 00:07:45,657
When the time comes, I will
see to it that you are...

90
00:07:47,158 --> 00:07:48,450
... duly rewarded.

91
00:07:49,158 --> 00:07:50,407
What is it?

92
00:07:50,408 --> 00:07:53,908
The siege engines. They've gone silent.

93
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,033
Get to safety!

94
00:08:05,450 --> 00:08:06,740
Push it!

95
00:08:06,741 --> 00:08:09,032
I said, push, you maggots.

96
00:08:12,366 --> 00:08:14,658
Push, come on, you maggots!

97
00:08:15,575 --> 00:08:16,991
Come on, you filth.

98
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:21,325
Put your stinkin' backs into it!

99
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:28,783
He's turning them away from the city.

100
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:37,866
Celebrimbor was more
mistaken than we knew.

101
00:08:39,783 --> 00:08:41,408
Prepare for ground assault.

102
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:44,449
Ground assault? From across the river?

103
00:09:04,741 --> 00:09:05,741
Again!

104
00:09:14,825 --> 00:09:16,366
They're damming the river.

105
00:09:43,575 --> 00:09:45,699
Prepare for ground assault!

106
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:47,366
To your positions!

107
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:49,199
Eregion is under siege.

108
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:52,575
The guards received that entreaty
from an Elf at the West-gate.

109
00:10:55,658 --> 00:10:57,866
Then they are more
desperate than we thought.

110
00:11:00,783 --> 00:11:04,657
I need the mine taken back, now.

111
00:11:04,658 --> 00:11:09,574
But, sire, your son is still
down there. And so is Princess...

112
00:11:09,575 --> 00:11:12,075
Every hour that we delay

113
00:11:13,241 --> 00:11:16,241
costs us unthinkable wealth.

114
00:11:18,866 --> 00:11:21,491
We must dig.

115
00:11:26,825 --> 00:11:27,825
Go!

116
00:11:33,825 --> 00:11:34,908
Here they come.

117
00:11:38,366 --> 00:11:40,365
Slow to learn, are you?

118
00:11:40,366 --> 00:11:43,408
Easy, lads. Just turn around.

119
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,200
No.

120
00:11:56,075 --> 00:11:58,116
We stand with you.

121
00:11:58,783 --> 00:11:59,866
Down your axes.

122
00:12:01,950 --> 00:12:04,601
That Ring has taken the King's heart.

123
00:12:04,602 --> 00:12:07,450
I will not let it take this mountain.

124
00:12:08,075 --> 00:12:09,450
We have to get it off him.

125
00:12:09,991 --> 00:12:12,241
Ours is not the only kingdom in peril.

126
00:12:13,450 --> 00:12:15,616
There's an Elf outside, wants your ear.

127
00:12:19,033 --> 00:12:20,033
Let him in.

128
00:12:20,991 --> 00:12:23,782
Well, we'll have to do it quietly.

129
00:12:23,783 --> 00:12:27,950
This particular Elf has been
banished from all Dwarven lands.

130
00:12:48,033 --> 00:12:49,033
Elrond.

131
00:12:51,158 --> 00:12:53,408
My heart sings to see you, old friend.

132
00:12:57,991 --> 00:13:02,657
You tidal-haired,
flowery-tongued flagpole.

133
00:13:02,658 --> 00:13:04,116
- "Tidal-haired"?
- Mm-hm!

134
00:13:09,158 --> 00:13:10,908
You've got some sand comin' here.

135
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:15,824
Have you any idea what I've
gone through since you left?

136
00:13:15,825 --> 00:13:18,991
It can hardly be more eventful
than what's transpired with me.

137
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:24,950
I'm about to overthrow my father.

138
00:13:38,991 --> 00:13:40,200
What've you got?

139
00:13:46,033 --> 00:13:47,033
Defeat.

140
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:51,450
Without your aid.

141
00:13:52,991 --> 00:13:55,283
Thousands of lives are at hazard, Durin.

142
00:13:55,950 --> 00:13:57,658
Celebrimbor is among them.

143
00:14:00,283 --> 00:14:04,116
I know I ask too much of you, Durin,
but I need your axe, old friend.

144
00:14:06,325 --> 00:14:07,783
I need it now.

145
00:14:26,783 --> 00:14:28,450
Move it!

146
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,783
Loose arrows!

147
00:15:32,408 --> 00:15:33,990
Hold fast!

148
00:15:33,991 --> 00:15:36,075
Captain, they have a Ravager.

149
00:15:38,616 --> 00:15:39,824
Prepare to fire!

150
00:15:39,825 --> 00:15:41,366
We must stop that machine!

151
00:15:59,783 --> 00:16:01,657
The Rings. Are they finished?

152
00:16:06,075 --> 00:16:07,075
Wait for it.

153
00:16:08,908 --> 00:16:09,908
Wait for what?

154
00:16:27,408 --> 00:16:28,491
Captivating.

155
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,491
It is a pattern.

156
00:16:32,575 --> 00:16:34,075
Do you not see? A cycle.

157
00:16:35,741 --> 00:16:38,824
Repeating itself at
intervals throughout the day.

158
00:16:38,825 --> 00:16:39,908
And there is more.

159
00:16:41,158 --> 00:16:42,158
Here.

160
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:45,490
Look. The embers...

161
00:16:45,491 --> 00:16:47,574
Celebrimbor, whatever so
inspired this epiphany,

162
00:16:47,575 --> 00:16:49,407
I assure you, we have
not the time for it.

163
00:16:49,408 --> 00:16:50,658
On the contrary,

164
00:16:52,491 --> 00:16:55,283
we would appear to have
all the time that we need.

165
00:17:00,825 --> 00:17:05,325
The candles... have not
burned an inch all day.

166
00:17:07,908 --> 00:17:09,325
You sought peace.

167
00:17:10,741 --> 00:17:12,575
I gave it to you.

168
00:17:13,575 --> 00:17:14,575
No.

169
00:17:15,866 --> 00:17:19,825
Whatever... Whatever this
is, this is hardly a gift.

170
00:17:23,366 --> 00:17:24,740
What have you done to me?

171
00:17:24,741 --> 00:17:25,825
Done to you?

172
00:17:27,116 --> 00:17:30,240
You welcomed my instruction.
You practically begged for it.

173
00:17:30,241 --> 00:17:34,116
Now, a... a mouse scurries
by, and you fly to pieces.

174
00:17:36,408 --> 00:17:37,408
Listen to yourself.

175
00:17:37,409 --> 00:17:39,366
Oh, what have you done to me?

176
00:17:41,741 --> 00:17:44,741
No Emissary of the Valar would do this.

177
00:17:47,116 --> 00:17:50,575
Who are you... truly?

178
00:17:51,491 --> 00:17:53,741
I am the one keeping the storm at bay.

179
00:17:55,283 --> 00:17:57,699
Balancing the very sun above your head.

180
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:02,200
All to give you this one
chance to prove your worth!

181
00:18:04,658 --> 00:18:07,449
Now, I want the Nine!

182
00:18:07,450 --> 00:18:08,700
No!

183
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:34,783
What...

184
00:19:45,533 --> 00:19:47,283
What... The mithril.

185
00:19:50,616 --> 00:19:53,533
What... What is... What is this?

186
00:19:55,283 --> 00:20:00,158
I have learned so much from
you, since I came to Eregion.

187
00:20:01,783 --> 00:20:05,783
But no lesson more lasting than this.

188
00:20:07,741 --> 00:20:09,533
True creation...

189
00:20:13,158 --> 00:20:14,991
requires sacrifice.

190
00:20:22,033 --> 00:20:23,325
You are He.

191
00:20:25,491 --> 00:20:26,825
Are you not?

192
00:20:28,533 --> 00:20:30,783
- You are...
- I have many names.

193
00:21:18,283 --> 00:21:19,450
Mirdania!

194
00:21:23,158 --> 00:21:25,574
Thank the Valar you're alive.

195
00:21:25,575 --> 00:21:28,324
We have been deceived. All of us.

196
00:21:28,325 --> 00:21:31,490
He planned all of this, to
force me to forge the Rings.

197
00:21:31,491 --> 00:21:35,575
He put me in some kind of a prison.
A prison of the mind. But I am out.

198
00:21:36,408 --> 00:21:37,740
I am out.

199
00:21:37,741 --> 00:21:41,907
He must've been distracted by
the siege, so he forgot the ruby.

200
00:21:41,908 --> 00:21:44,740
And the mouse. The same mouse...

201
00:21:44,741 --> 00:21:46,116
And...

202
00:21:47,158 --> 00:21:49,366
You must... You must believe me.

203
00:21:51,241 --> 00:21:53,033
You have to believe me!

204
00:22:00,908 --> 00:22:02,908
This is the thinnest part of the wall.

205
00:22:05,491 --> 00:22:06,532
Come on!

206
00:22:11,616 --> 00:22:15,325
We have to brace the
foundations! Quickly, now!

207
00:22:22,491 --> 00:22:23,491
Seize him.

208
00:22:25,616 --> 00:22:26,991
He is Sauron.

209
00:22:28,908 --> 00:22:30,075
Seize him!

210
00:22:31,533 --> 00:22:34,866
He has been lying to you all along.

211
00:22:36,741 --> 00:22:39,240
No. He has been protecting us.

212
00:22:39,241 --> 00:22:42,115
While you've been in your tower,
giving orders that might have been

213
00:22:42,116 --> 00:22:43,199
the end of us all.

214
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:45,741
No. No, that was him.

215
00:22:46,908 --> 00:22:48,491
He is Sauron!

216
00:22:50,158 --> 00:22:54,450
If you do not believe me, cut him open.

217
00:22:56,158 --> 00:22:58,366
Look at his hand, look at his blood.

218
00:22:59,075 --> 00:23:00,658
Black as pitch.

219
00:23:13,950 --> 00:23:15,074
Come, my lord.

220
00:23:15,075 --> 00:23:17,074
Let's get you back where you belong.

221
00:23:17,075 --> 00:23:18,657
Get your hands off me!

222
00:23:18,658 --> 00:23:21,241
No!

223
00:23:43,950 --> 00:23:45,033
All this can end.

224
00:23:47,866 --> 00:23:52,075
Finish the Nine, and
I will spare your city.

225
00:23:57,075 --> 00:23:58,575
What will you do with them?

226
00:24:00,866 --> 00:24:04,033
Create a perfect and lasting peace.

227
00:24:37,908 --> 00:24:39,241
Come on!

228
00:25:16,075 --> 00:25:17,908
Death to our foes!

229
00:26:29,408 --> 00:26:30,408
Halt!

230
00:26:40,325 --> 00:26:44,033
Welcome, Commander Elrond.

231
00:26:55,033 --> 00:26:56,408
The Ring you carry.

232
00:26:58,908 --> 00:26:59,908
Show it to me.

233
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:03,033
A foolish act if I had brought it here.

234
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:06,283
You are a courtier.

235
00:27:07,241 --> 00:27:09,699
More suited to wielding
a scroll than a sword.

236
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:11,324
You've never seen me wield either.

237
00:27:11,325 --> 00:27:13,407
You should've just
kept charging, Elrond.

238
00:27:13,408 --> 00:27:16,949
If she speaks again, cut out her tongue.

239
00:27:21,741 --> 00:27:25,491
Sauron is my enemy as much as yours.

240
00:27:26,533 --> 00:27:30,032
Give me what I need to defeat
him and let us all be rid of him.

241
00:27:30,033 --> 00:27:33,240
Is it not you that has done his
bidding by laying siege to Eregion?

242
00:27:33,241 --> 00:27:35,825
Eregion has fallen into shadow.

243
00:27:36,908 --> 00:27:42,032
It belongs to the Deceiver now,
as does every Elf within its walls.

244
00:27:42,033 --> 00:27:43,657
Not Lord Celebrimbor.

245
00:27:43,658 --> 00:27:47,908
It was Celebrimbor himself
who welcomed Sauron in.

246
00:27:49,158 --> 00:27:50,658
You cannot save him.

247
00:27:52,200 --> 00:27:53,991
You can save Galadriel.

248
00:27:57,741 --> 00:27:59,325
It is an earnest offer.

249
00:28:00,866 --> 00:28:02,366
I suggest you take it.

250
00:28:03,491 --> 00:28:05,575
And leave Sauron to me.

251
00:28:12,491 --> 00:28:15,991
You have the beauty of your
foremother, Melian of the Valar.

252
00:28:17,491 --> 00:28:21,116
If even a fragment of her
wisdom is in your veins,

253
00:28:22,283 --> 00:28:25,075
you must know you cannot
defeat me in battle.

254
00:28:26,616 --> 00:28:28,450
I will outmaneuver you,

255
00:28:28,991 --> 00:28:34,200
my forces outfight
yours, and you will fall.

256
00:28:35,575 --> 00:28:38,741
Not before you have painted
the sands of the Glanduin black

257
00:28:39,575 --> 00:28:41,115
with the blood of your kin.

258
00:28:42,533 --> 00:28:44,699
My children have endured cruelties

259
00:28:44,700 --> 00:28:48,158
your bravest couldn't
bear to hear spoken aloud.

260
00:28:49,325 --> 00:28:53,616
Are you prepared to spend
their lives so freely, Adar?

261
00:28:56,950 --> 00:28:58,116
Are they?

262
00:29:04,950 --> 00:29:09,908
The Ring for Galadriel's
life. What is it to be?

263
00:29:23,908 --> 00:29:25,741
Ask me on the field,

264
00:29:26,741 --> 00:29:29,157
when the neck with a
blade against it is yours.

265
00:29:34,325 --> 00:29:35,325
Very well.

266
00:29:39,700 --> 00:29:41,116
I will meet you there...

267
00:29:44,325 --> 00:29:46,408
with her head on a pike.

268
00:29:50,366 --> 00:29:53,575
If that is to be the way of things,
I should like to bid her farewell.

269
00:29:57,825 --> 00:29:59,033
He's unarmed.

270
00:30:17,575 --> 00:30:18,825
Forgive me.

271
00:30:23,741 --> 00:30:24,908
Win.

272
00:30:59,325 --> 00:31:00,491
Vorohil.

273
00:31:06,533 --> 00:31:10,200
The enemy outnumber us ten
to one. So why the confidence?

274
00:31:11,158 --> 00:31:13,782
Because I know something the
Father of the Orcs does not.

275
00:31:13,783 --> 00:31:14,907
And what is that?

276
00:31:14,908 --> 00:31:17,150
Even now Prince Durin is rallying

277
00:31:17,151 --> 00:31:18,408
a legion of Dwarves to our aid.

278
00:31:19,158 --> 00:31:21,200
And at the first rays of sunlight...

279
00:31:22,033 --> 00:31:25,700
... you will guide them
straight into Adar's flank.

280
00:31:27,116 --> 00:31:28,116
Outstanding.

281
00:31:32,866 --> 00:31:33,866
Ride to them now.

282
00:31:36,158 --> 00:31:38,282
Meantime, I will ensure
that Eregion's walls

283
00:31:38,283 --> 00:31:39,700
hold for one more night.

284
00:31:56,075 --> 00:31:58,866
Warriors of Khazad-dûm.

285
00:32:04,658 --> 00:32:06,325
At this moment,

286
00:32:07,533 --> 00:32:11,700
the great tale of our
Age is being written.

287
00:32:15,158 --> 00:32:20,532
And it falls to us to
decide whether it will end

288
00:32:20,533 --> 00:32:26,408
in tragedy... or triumph.

289
00:32:31,116 --> 00:32:33,575
Sauron the Stoneheart,

290
00:32:35,866 --> 00:32:38,400
who stole the seven smithing secrets

291
00:32:38,401 --> 00:32:41,866
from our forebearers, has returned.

292
00:32:42,950 --> 00:32:48,866
Forging Rings to enslave
us and all of Middle-earth.

293
00:32:49,825 --> 00:32:52,283
The Elves cannot defeat him.

294
00:32:54,491 --> 00:32:55,908
Not without us.

295
00:33:03,950 --> 00:33:05,950
And Sauron knows this.

296
00:33:07,575 --> 00:33:12,866
He thinks, by stoking our greed,

297
00:33:14,700 --> 00:33:17,866
he can turn our hearts to ash

298
00:33:19,116 --> 00:33:23,116
and sweep us from the
field without a fight.

299
00:33:28,866 --> 00:33:32,324
But we are stronger than he knows.

300
00:33:32,325 --> 00:33:33,865
Aye!

301
00:33:33,866 --> 00:33:38,324
For there is something
all Dwarves prize,

302
00:33:38,325 --> 00:33:41,199
far more than riches.

303
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:45,033
More even than this
mountain we hold dear.

304
00:33:46,700 --> 00:33:51,658
Fight with me, so all the world can see,

305
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:54,365
that Dwarven loyalty

306
00:33:54,366 --> 00:33:59,907
is a force stronger than any sorcery!

307
00:33:59,908 --> 00:34:00,990
Aye!

308
00:34:00,991 --> 00:34:03,490
More powerful than any army!

309
00:34:03,491 --> 00:34:04,824
Aye!

310
00:34:04,825 --> 00:34:08,949
Deeper than the bones of the earth!

311
00:34:08,950 --> 00:34:10,491
Aye!

312
00:34:11,366 --> 00:34:14,324
Will you fight with our friends?

313
00:34:14,325 --> 00:34:15,574
Aye!

314
00:34:15,575 --> 00:34:19,532
Will you fight for Khazad-dûm?

315
00:34:19,533 --> 00:34:22,907
Baruk Khazâd! Baruk Khazâd!

316
00:34:22,908 --> 00:34:30,908
Baruk Khazâd! Baruk Khazâd!

317
00:34:36,408 --> 00:34:38,115
Khazad...

318
00:34:38,116 --> 00:34:40,240
Dûm!

319
00:34:40,241 --> 00:34:43,365
We march for Eregion!

320
00:34:52,533 --> 00:34:53,783
Defend the city!

321
00:35:09,408 --> 00:35:10,408
To the wall!

322
00:35:10,991 --> 00:35:11,991
To the wall!

323
00:35:48,116 --> 00:35:50,325
Gonna spill your guts, Elf.

324
00:35:56,283 --> 00:35:57,283
Die.

325
00:36:01,450 --> 00:36:05,075
No! No! No, no! No!

326
00:36:42,241 --> 00:36:43,658
That's enough!

327
00:36:55,741 --> 00:36:58,741
Again! Reset the Ravager!

328
00:37:00,241 --> 00:37:01,325
Move!

329
00:37:04,991 --> 00:37:06,200
Lord-father.

330
00:37:07,241 --> 00:37:09,657
The wall is stronger than we thought.

331
00:37:09,658 --> 00:37:11,741
We may not breach it before morning.

332
00:37:12,491 --> 00:37:15,407
The Elf is faring
better than you expected.

333
00:37:15,408 --> 00:37:19,157
His troops have already
destroyed five of our trebuchets.

334
00:37:19,158 --> 00:37:20,950
Many Uruk are dying.

335
00:37:21,908 --> 00:37:23,782
What are your orders, Lord-father?

336
00:37:23,783 --> 00:37:26,116
- Shall we sound the retreat?
- No.

337
00:37:28,491 --> 00:37:30,075
Sauron must not escape.

338
00:37:31,700 --> 00:37:35,699
Bring down that wall. At any cost.

339
00:37:35,700 --> 00:37:36,741
Adar!

340
00:37:41,116 --> 00:37:45,491
You told us... you loved us.

341
00:37:46,575 --> 00:37:48,616
With all that is left of my heart.

342
00:37:50,950 --> 00:37:55,116
Too much, to let you
become Sauron's slaves.

343
00:38:10,658 --> 00:38:11,658
Hurry!

344
00:38:17,325 --> 00:38:20,450
She's still in the camp. Find her!

345
00:38:54,283 --> 00:38:55,325
He's dead.

346
00:38:56,241 --> 00:38:57,241
He's gone.

347
00:38:58,325 --> 00:39:01,741
Eh. You there! Come here and help.

348
00:39:06,866 --> 00:39:07,866
He's dead.

349
00:39:59,033 --> 00:40:01,325
In flames they return to darkness.

350
00:40:04,283 --> 00:40:06,491
In flames they return to darkness.

351
00:40:33,700 --> 00:40:36,866
Look at that pretty hair.

352
00:41:02,366 --> 00:41:04,825
Whatever force it was that
brought you here, soldier,

353
00:41:05,700 --> 00:41:07,158
I am grateful for it.

354
00:41:07,575 --> 00:41:11,990
Come, I know a hidden way into
the city. We must find Sauron.

355
00:41:11,991 --> 00:41:13,491
I'm here for him.

356
00:41:18,450 --> 00:41:22,700
Try to move against him now,
the cost will be your life.

357
00:41:25,075 --> 00:41:26,325
He can have it.

358
00:41:28,908 --> 00:41:31,200
He has taken everything else from me.

359
00:41:34,116 --> 00:41:35,325
Arondir.

360
00:41:37,991 --> 00:41:41,200
There is a dearth of
Elven heroes this night.

361
00:41:43,116 --> 00:41:46,825
It would be a pity to lose another.

362
00:41:48,825 --> 00:41:51,616
And the true fight with
Adar will come later.

363
00:42:07,533 --> 00:42:09,865
The army has assembled at
the West-gate, Prince Durin.

364
00:42:09,866 --> 00:42:11,157
Good.

365
00:42:11,158 --> 00:42:13,200
Durin!

366
00:42:15,491 --> 00:42:16,491
Prince Durin!

367
00:42:18,825 --> 00:42:19,866
Wait!

368
00:42:24,700 --> 00:42:28,575
Your father, he turned
his axe on my men.

369
00:42:30,783 --> 00:42:33,615
He cut through them
like stalks of wheat.

370
00:42:35,658 --> 00:42:37,491
But he's gonna dig.

371
00:42:38,200 --> 00:42:40,199
He's gonna loose that beast!

372
00:42:40,200 --> 00:42:42,574
- Disa, is she...
- I don't know.

373
00:42:42,575 --> 00:42:44,782
But she sent me to find you.

374
00:42:44,783 --> 00:42:47,575
She says you have to recall the army.

375
00:42:48,075 --> 00:42:49,533
And what about Elrond?

376
00:42:50,658 --> 00:42:52,950
You take that army to Eregion now,

377
00:42:53,741 --> 00:42:56,241
and Khazad-dûm might not
be here when you return.

378
00:43:12,366 --> 00:43:16,450
Be not afraid. This too shall pass.

379
00:43:19,241 --> 00:43:23,199
I promise you, when
Middle-earth is healed,

380
00:43:23,200 --> 00:43:25,825
and its people see what
you and I did here...

381
00:43:29,200 --> 00:43:31,241
all our sufferings will be worth it.

382
00:43:32,783 --> 00:43:33,783
"Our sufferings"?

383
00:43:34,450 --> 00:43:38,324
You must know it pains
me, treating you like...

384
00:43:38,325 --> 00:43:40,491
Like you've treated countless others?

385
00:43:45,075 --> 00:43:46,491
Like Morgoth treated me.

386
00:43:49,408 --> 00:43:52,408
Do you know what it is to be
tortured at the hands of a god?

387
00:43:54,783 --> 00:43:56,200
I cannot imagine.

388
00:43:57,866 --> 00:44:01,033
I see the end, Celebrimbor.

389
00:44:02,616 --> 00:44:03,741
So clearly.

390
00:44:04,991 --> 00:44:07,158
I have seen it from the moment I awoke.

391
00:44:08,616 --> 00:44:12,616
But his end, it was different from mine.

392
00:44:15,200 --> 00:44:21,158
For what he wished to destroy,
I wished... to perfect.

393
00:44:24,408 --> 00:44:28,783
Sometimes, the pain
almost became a reward.

394
00:44:29,575 --> 00:44:31,033
Became a game.

395
00:44:32,533 --> 00:44:36,366
A contest, to see whose
will was the mightier.

396
00:44:38,491 --> 00:44:40,181
And after all that,
you would still choose

397
00:44:40,182 --> 00:44:42,907
to inflict the same pain upon me?

398
00:44:42,908 --> 00:44:43,991
No.

399
00:44:51,200 --> 00:44:52,783
You chose it.

400
00:44:55,033 --> 00:44:56,158
Not I.

401
00:44:58,450 --> 00:44:59,450
What?

402
00:45:02,991 --> 00:45:07,533
All depends... on the Rings.

403
00:45:08,908 --> 00:45:11,824
And since you forced me

404
00:45:11,825 --> 00:45:15,658
to torment you to bring them into being,

405
00:45:17,866 --> 00:45:20,158
I am but a victim of your obstinance.

406
00:45:22,450 --> 00:45:26,950
And you, the true author
of your own torment.

407
00:45:35,033 --> 00:45:37,033
You truly are the Great Deceiver.

408
00:45:42,116 --> 00:45:44,033
You can deceive even yourself.

409
00:45:48,491 --> 00:45:49,908
Finish them.

410
00:46:40,325 --> 00:46:41,616
Release!

411
00:47:04,741 --> 00:47:05,741
Hurry!

412
00:47:32,658 --> 00:47:33,741
Fire!

413
00:48:53,116 --> 00:48:56,950
Whose will is the mightier?

414
00:49:51,158 --> 00:49:53,032
Look what he's done to himself.

415
00:49:53,033 --> 00:49:55,200
The old fool really has gone mad.

416
00:49:55,866 --> 00:49:59,783
You are to remain in the tower, so
as not to be a danger to yourself.

417
00:50:00,491 --> 00:50:04,200
By order of Annatar. Lord of Eregion.

418
00:50:12,783 --> 00:50:13,908
Release him.

419
00:50:15,116 --> 00:50:16,116
My lady?

420
00:50:17,450 --> 00:50:22,700
That is Lord Celebrimbor.
Greatest of Elven-smiths.

421
00:50:24,200 --> 00:50:26,199
- Release him.
- But the Lord of Eregion ordered...

422
00:50:26,200 --> 00:50:28,575
This is the Lord of Eregion.

423
00:50:38,950 --> 00:50:42,200
Celebrimbor, it's me.

424
00:50:49,283 --> 00:50:50,491
Celebrimbor.

425
00:50:51,366 --> 00:50:52,950
When I saw you,

426
00:50:54,116 --> 00:50:57,075
for a moment, I was certain that
you were but another illusion,

427
00:50:58,700 --> 00:51:02,699
another cruelty devised to
torment me with false hope.

428
00:51:02,700 --> 00:51:03,908
Sauron?

429
00:51:06,158 --> 00:51:07,490
More Rings?

430
00:51:07,491 --> 00:51:08,825
Nine.

431
00:51:10,950 --> 00:51:15,366
Nine Rings to enslave the world of Men.

432
00:51:15,950 --> 00:51:19,700
As he... enslaved me.

433
00:51:21,366 --> 00:51:23,824
I... It was my fault.

434
00:51:23,825 --> 00:51:24,908
No!

435
00:51:25,825 --> 00:51:29,700
From the beginning,
a part of me... knew.

436
00:51:30,325 --> 00:51:33,991
A part of me saw. But I...
I wanted what he offered.

437
00:51:35,075 --> 00:51:40,241
So, I, I blinded myself
to, to what he was.

438
00:51:42,575 --> 00:51:43,908
So did I.

439
00:51:48,325 --> 00:51:50,324
- It is him.
- Hurry.

440
00:51:50,325 --> 00:51:54,532
The old Dwarven tunnel. I used
it to enter the city undetected.

441
00:51:54,533 --> 00:51:56,949
It will bear you and
the Rings far from here.

442
00:51:56,950 --> 00:51:58,032
No. No.

443
00:51:58,033 --> 00:51:59,407
Go! Now!

444
00:51:59,408 --> 00:52:01,574
I cannot. It must be you.

445
00:52:01,575 --> 00:52:04,490
He will realize what has happened.
He will come for the Rings.

446
00:52:04,491 --> 00:52:09,533
I will ensure it is some time
before that comes to pass.

447
00:52:10,700 --> 00:52:15,615
Take the Rings, save anyone
in the city you can. Hurry!

448
00:52:15,616 --> 00:52:16,783
No.

449
00:52:18,033 --> 00:52:20,282
I won't let you face him alone!

450
00:52:20,283 --> 00:52:23,116
I... I built this city.

451
00:52:25,033 --> 00:52:26,783
My place is here.

452
00:52:27,991 --> 00:52:29,825
And he will not be alone.

453
00:52:39,116 --> 00:52:42,200
I'm sorry. I brought him here.

454
00:52:44,450 --> 00:52:46,658
I'm sorry I wasn't stronger.

455
00:52:47,158 --> 00:52:49,158
Neither of us was strong enough.

456
00:52:50,491 --> 00:52:53,241
There might not be anyone
in Middle-earth who is.

457
00:52:54,950 --> 00:52:59,450
But perhaps, the Elves
need only remember

458
00:53:00,866 --> 00:53:04,700
that it is not strength
that overcomes darkness,

459
00:53:06,491 --> 00:53:07,741
but light.

460
00:53:08,700 --> 00:53:10,450
Armies may rise,

461
00:53:12,950 --> 00:53:14,907
hearts may fail,

462
00:53:14,908 --> 00:53:20,907
yet still, light endures,
and is mightier than strength.

463
00:53:25,158 --> 00:53:30,657
For in its presence,
all darkness must flee.

464
00:53:36,575 --> 00:53:37,991
Namarië.

465
00:54:19,741 --> 00:54:22,075
Again! We're almost there!

466
00:54:32,575 --> 00:54:35,157
They'll breach the wall
soon, Commander. Won't they?

467
00:54:35,158 --> 00:54:38,574
No, Rían! Our enemy
will not breach that wall!

468
00:54:38,575 --> 00:54:41,325
A single arrow from you
may yet turn the tide.

469
00:54:42,533 --> 00:54:45,449
- How many torch arrows do you have left?
- Enough to do my part.

470
00:54:45,450 --> 00:54:47,032
All I need is a clear line of sight.

471
00:54:47,033 --> 00:54:48,325
Follow me.

472
00:54:50,116 --> 00:54:51,116
Go!

473
00:55:02,991 --> 00:55:04,283
Take the shot!

474
00:55:10,158 --> 00:55:11,158
No.

475
00:55:52,866 --> 00:55:54,282
Dagranno!

476
00:56:14,200 --> 00:56:15,200
Destroy it!

477
00:56:26,866 --> 00:56:28,158
Send him in.

478
00:56:29,241 --> 00:56:33,783
Lord-father, he will kill our own kind.

479
00:56:34,575 --> 00:56:36,116
Send him in.

480
00:56:55,700 --> 00:56:58,033
The Orcs, they're fleeing!

481
00:57:01,450 --> 00:57:04,366
No. They're clearing a path.

482
00:57:35,325 --> 00:57:37,158
You shall not find them here.

483
00:57:38,366 --> 00:57:40,783
They will be far from your reach by now.

484
00:57:46,116 --> 00:57:50,574
Then you are going to bring them
to me and place them in my hand.

485
00:57:50,575 --> 00:57:53,158
Your hand will never
touch another Ring again.

486
00:58:09,533 --> 00:58:11,782
By order of the true Lord of Eregion,

487
00:58:11,783 --> 00:58:13,532
you, Sauron, are hereby...

488
00:58:20,283 --> 00:58:23,450
You think it was only you,
who put yourself in my power?

489
00:59:02,408 --> 00:59:04,408
You will give me the Nine.

490
00:59:18,491 --> 00:59:21,033
It must not reach the wall!

491
01:00:02,616 --> 01:00:03,616
Watch out!

492
01:00:18,200 --> 01:00:19,825
Commander, look out!

493
01:00:27,950 --> 01:00:30,240
Kill it now!

494
01:01:26,866 --> 01:01:29,158
Go back to your hill and be buried.

495
01:01:42,658 --> 01:01:43,865
Commander!

496
01:02:15,158 --> 01:02:16,324
Commander.

497
01:02:16,325 --> 01:02:17,533
High King.

498
01:02:18,575 --> 01:02:19,865
You should not be here.

499
01:02:19,866 --> 01:02:22,533
A king's place is wherever
the need is greatest.

500
01:02:37,533 --> 01:02:41,949
My children! March with me!

501
01:03:28,866 --> 01:03:31,324
The Dwarves! The Dwarves are coming!

502
01:03:31,325 --> 01:03:32,825
Look to the north!

503
01:03:49,616 --> 01:03:50,616
Vorohil.

504
01:03:56,325 --> 01:03:58,366
Durin recalled their army.

505
01:04:00,200 --> 01:04:02,074
The gate of Khazad-dûm is shut.

506
01:04:02,075 --> 01:04:06,408
No, there... must be some mistake.

507
01:04:09,908 --> 01:04:10,991
Durin will come!

508
01:04:28,116 --> 01:04:30,032
Form ranks!

509
01:04:32,908 --> 01:04:33,908
Durin will come.

510
01:04:40,200 --> 01:04:42,115
Kill them all!

511
01:04:45,450 --> 01:04:47,490
Attack!

512
01:04:55,616 --> 01:04:56,866
Durin will come.

513
01:05:03,033 --> 01:05:04,532
Durin will come.

514
01:07:08,325 --> 01:07:10,408
Have you forgotten your Rúmil?

515
01:07:17,200 --> 01:07:19,450
"Never make war in anger."

516
01:07:39,076 --> 01:07:44,076
- Synced and corrected by <font color="#009BCB"><b>chamallow</b></font> -
